    "q-68218": {
      "dom_id": "step-q68218",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "The relationship between the variables $h$ and $t$ is shown in the following table:\n\n| $t$ | $h$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $4$ | $8$ |\n| $5$ | $15$ |\n| $6$ | $24$ |\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. There is **not** a proportional relationship between $h$ and $t.$\n\nII. The constant of proportionality is $6.$\n\nIII. There is a proportional relationship between $h$ and $t.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's add a new column to our table and compute the ratio $\\frac{h}{t}:$\n\n| $t$ | $h$ | $\\frac{h}{t}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $4$ | $8$ | $2$ |\n| $5$ | $15$ | $3$ |\n| $6$ | $24$ | $4$ |\n\nThe ratio $\\frac{h}{t}$ is not the same for each row. Therefore, there is *not* a proportional relationship between $h$ and $t.$ Consequently, there is no constant of proportionality.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-68218-a",
              "type": "text",
              "value": "I only",
              "html": "I only"
            },
            {
              "option": "b",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-68218-b",
              "type": "text",
              "value": "II and III only",
              "html": "II and III only"
            },
            {
              "option": "c",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-68218-c",
